      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "FormL4: Dataset Construction",
      "pageStart": 3,
      "pageEnd": 3,
      "target": "../sections/sec-002-forml4-dataset-construction.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "The rapid development of Lean 4 (de Moura & Ullrich, 2021) necessitates a benchmark to assess\nLLMs’ autoformalization capabilities. Existing datasets (Jiang et al., 2023a; Ying et al., 2024a) aims\nto create benchmarks by informalizing formal theorems from existing libraries. However, they rely\non zero-shot instructions to collect natural language statements from GPT-4 without quality checks\nor rigorous post-processing. Additionally, it focuses solely on translating theorems, overlooking the\nbenefits of using proofs as context, which could enhance both the dataset quality and the evaluation\nof",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Motivates the FORML4 benchmark by noting that existing Lean 4 autoformalization datasets rely on unchecked zero-shot GPT-4 informalization of theorem statements alone and omit proofs as context for dataset quality and evaluation.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-10-28"
      }
