      "narrative": null,
      "content": "of the Lean 4 compiler (Section 4.2).\n4.1\nVERIFICATION MODEL\nWe propose to train the verifier by leveraging the granular, process-level feedback provided by the\nLean 4 compiler. This method diverges from previous approaches (Wu et al., 2022) that rely solely\non binary compilation outcomes. Instead, we employ a more nuanced strategy that assigns labels\nto each step in the training data based on the “first error location” principle introduced by Uesato\net al. (2022). Our labeling strategy is as follows: steps preceding the first compiler-detected error are\nlabeled as “correct”, while subsequent",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Formulates the verification models and notation (Table 3), contrasting an Outcome-Supervised Verifier (OSV) trained with uniform final-compilation labels against a Process-Supervised Verifier (PSV) trained with step-level cross-entropy loss using \"first error location\" labels from the Lean 4 compiler.",
        "state": "draft",
